WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:05.791
In professional life,

2
00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:09.791
if you are in a leadership position,

3
00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:11.958
making the right choice

4
00:00:11.958 --> 00:00:15.416
becomes extremely important.

5
00:00:15.416 --> 00:00:18.833
Many such situations will arise

6
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:23.500
when you must choose one of two people.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.708
For example,

8
00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:27.583
if a disagreement arises between two people,

9
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:30.500
when an important task must be assigned,

10
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.166
when selecting someone for a promotion,

11
00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:37.208
many such situations will arise.

12
00:00:37.208 --> 00:00:39.375
A good leader

13
00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:42.708
cannot take personal sides in such cases,

14
00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:46.291
because bias will, like a termite,

15
00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:50.291
hollow out an organisation.

16
00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:52.125
So what should be done?

17
00:00:52.125 --> 00:00:53.458
Such decisions

18
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:56.416
must be based on clear principles.

19
00:00:56.416 --> 00:01:01.166
They must be based on the
values of the organisation.

20
00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:03.250
When Arjun asked

21
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.958
whether, in devotion,

22
00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:08.708
worship of the personal form is superior,

23
00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:13.000
or contemplation and meditation
on the formless,

24
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.500
My answer was very clear.

25
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.333
This was not a personal side,

26
00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:25.083
but behind it there is also a sound principle,

27
00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:28.000
which became clear in the later verses too.

28
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.708
In the same way,

29
00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:32.666
the work of those appointed
to leadership positions

30
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:35.625
is not to take personal sides, but

31
00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:37.625
to make clear decisions

32
00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:39.625
according to sound principles

33
00:01:39.625 --> 00:01:42.958
and to give clear answers to colleagues.

34
00:01:42.958 --> 00:01:44.125
And if

35
00:01:44.125 --> 00:01:45.583
your decisions

36
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:49.333
align with the values of the organisation,

37
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:53.291
you will not be unsettled by worry

38
00:01:53.291 --> 00:01:57.250
that your answer may upset someone,

39
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.208
because even the person you do not choose

40
00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:04.125
you will be able to show,
what they need to improve

41
00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:07.125
to grow within the organisation,

42
00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:09.041
according to the principles.

43
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:12.166
This is only possible because

44
00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:16.333
your decision was based on the right values.

45
00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:17.541
In such a case,

46
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:21.583
your colleagues' trust in you will also grow.

47
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:23.375
Remember,

48
00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:26.458
not personal preference, but

49
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:30.166
according to the principles
and values of the organisation,

50
00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:31.416
make your decisions.
